
== S0  transcription of the landed tables
PASS S0.tables  [source] landed sgn, pc, pt, phiW, idW, chainW, reflY match this script's transcription

== S1  the dictionary facts the reductions use (re-derived here; the landed probe replay covers D1-D7, F0-F10)
PASS D1  [identity] pauliW (cnot w) = CNOT pauliW(w) CNOT^dagger, symbolic w
PASS D5  [identity] pauliW (prodState x y) = rho(x) (x) rho(y), symbolic
PASS D6  [identity] rho(x) is Hermitian with trace 1 and det (1 - |x|^2)/4 (so PSD iff |x| <= 1)
PASS Dpt  [identity] pauliW (actT reflY w) = partial transpose (second qubit) of pauliW(w), symbolic: twin = PT2(Q3)
PASS Dtr  [identity] pauliW (actC reflY (actT reflY w)) = pauliW(w)^T, symbolic (full transpose; so actC reflY Q3 = transpose(actT reflY Q3) = twin)
PASS Dmax  [identity] pairVal a b (actT R w) = pairVal a (homMap R^T b) w and pairVal a b (actC R w) = pairVal (homMap R^T a) b w, symbolic R (orthogonal R preserve the Lorentz cone L, so maxCone is invariant under actC R, actT R)
PASS DL  [identity] homMap reflY preserves the Lorentz form b0^2 - |b|^2 and b0 (so it maps L onto L)
PASS Dadj  [identity] ipW (actT reflY E) X = ipW E (actT reflY X), symbolic (so dualW (actT reflY K) = actT reflY (dualW K))
PASS Dsep  [identity] actT reflY (prodState x y) = prodState x (reflY y) and |reflY y|^2 = |y|^2 (SEP is actT reflY-invariant; so is the ball)
PASS Dloc  [identity] actC M (actT M' (prodState x y)) = prodState (M x) (M' y), symbolic M, M' (local maps send products to products; orthogonal ones keep the ball, so they preserve SEP)
PASS Dorth  [identity] |R^T b|^2 = b^T (R R^T) b, symbolic R, b (so orthogonal R keep the Lorentz cone L; with Dmax every local orthogonal map preserves maxCone)
PASS Dpv  [identity] pairVal a b w = ipW (a b^T) w, symbolic: SEP* = maxCone and maxCone* = SEP read through tables

== S2  the four gates: N-CLASS form, inverse, orientation bit
PASS G.g_cnot  [identity] g_cnot: N = actC A actT B cnot actC A' actT B' with orthogonal locals; the stated inverse is a two-sided inverse; orient(A, B) = False
PASS G.g_D  [identity] g_D: N = actC A actT B cnot actC A' actT B' with orthogonal locals; the stated inverse is a two-sided inverse; orient(A, B) = True
PASS G.g_pre  [identity] g_pre: N = actC A actT B cnot actC A' actT B' with orthogonal locals; the stated inverse is a two-sided inverse; orient(A, B) = False
PASS G.g_Tw  [identity] g_Tw: N = actC A actT B cnot actC A' actT B' with orthogonal locals; the stated inverse is a two-sided inverse; orient(A, B) = True
PASS G.orient  [enumerate] orientation bits: g_cnot false, g_D true, g_pre false, g_Tw true
PASS G.cc  [countercontrol] countercontrol: actT reflY . cnot is not of N-CLASS form with B = I (the post-local is read)

== S3  membership witnesses (decisive for every "fails" cell)
PASS W1  [witness] phiW in Q3 (pauliW phiW is PSD: all principal minors >= 0)
PASS W2  [witness] idW not in Q3: the singlet value of pauliW idW is -1
PASS W2t  [witness] idW in twin: actT reflY idW = phiW in Q3
PASS W3  [witness] phiW not in twin: actT reflY phiW = idW, not in Q3 (W2)
PASS W4  [witness] chainW not in maxCone: pairVal at the sharp effects of -e1, -e3 (both in L) is -1/2
PASS W5  [witness] dg(1,-1,1,-1) in maxCone (pairVal = a0 b0 - a1 b1 + a2 b2 - a3 b3 >= a0 b0 - |a||b| >= 0 by Cauchy-Schwarz) and ipW phiW dg(1,-1,1,-1) = -2: phiW not in dualW maxCone
PASS W6  [witness] dg(1,-1,-1,-1) in Q3 (pauliW = singlet projector, PSD) and ipW idW dg(1,-1,-1,-1) = -2: idW not in dualW Q3
PASS W7  [witness] phiW not in SEP: F = dg(1,-1,1,-1) has ipW F (prodState x y) = |x - D y|^2/2 + (1-|x|^2)/2 + (1-|y|^2)/2 (>= 0 on the ball; D = diag(1,-1,1)) and ipW F phiW = -2
PASS W8  [witness] idW not in SEP: F' = dg(1,-1,-1,-1) has ipW F' (prodState x y) = |x - y|^2/2 + (1-|x|^2)/2 + (1-|y|^2)/2 and ipW F' idW = -2
PASS W9  [identity] phiW and idW lie in maxCone = SEP*: pairVal a b phiW = a0b0 + a1b1 - a2b2 + a3b3 and pairVal a b idW = a0b0 + a.b, each >= a0 b0 - |a||b| >= 0 (Cauchy-Schwarz)
PASS W10  [witness] dg(2,-1,1,-1) = E00 + dg(1,-1,1,-1) lies in int maxCone (pairVal >= a0 b0 > 0 on nonzero L x L) and ipW phiW dg(2,-1,1,-1) = -1: phiW not in dualW Kint
PASS W11  [witness] prodState xplus z3 lies in twin: actT reflY fixes it (reflY z3 = z3) and it lies in Q3 (D5, D6)
PASS W12  [witness] chains: cnot idW = chainW; actT reflY chainW = chainW; g_D: pxz -> idW -> chainW; g_pre: pxz -> phiW -> chainW; g_Tw: phiW -> chainW; g_D^-1 phiW = chainW; g_pre^-1 pxz = idW
PASS W13  [witness] the M_D gate puts the M_Q Bell table off Q3: bellOf(I, reflY) = actT reflY phiW = idW (W2)
PASS W14  [identity] pre-corrections: g_D . actT reflY = g_Tw and g_pre . actT reflY = cnot (symbolic); cnot pxz = phiW
PASS W.cc  [countercontrol] countercontrol: the twin Bell table idW is in twin (W2t) while the Q3 Bell table phiW is not (W3): the cone and the post-local must match

== S4  gate images of product states and the link family (reductions for the "holds" cells)
PASS P1  [identity] g_D (prodState x y) = actT reflY (cnot (prodState x y)) and g_D^-1 (prodState x y) = cnot (prodState x (reflY y))
PASS P2  [identity] g_pre (prodState x y) = cnot (prodState x (reflY y)) and g_pre^-1 = actT reflY . cnot
PASS P3  [identity] g_Tw (prodState x y) = actT reflY (cnot (prodState x (reflY y))) and g_Tw is an involution
PASS L1  [identity] link tables with post-locals (I, I): actC (Rz Rx) phiW = cnot (prodState (Rz xplus) (Rx z3)), symbolic angles (so they lie in Q3 by D1, D5, D6)
PASS L2  [identity] link tables with post-locals (I, reflY): actC (Rz Rx) (actT reflY phiW) = actT reflY (actC (Rz Rx) phiW) (so they lie in twin)
PASS L3  [sample] sample: at m1 = 1/2, m2 = 1/3 the (I, I) link table is in Q3 and its actT reflY image is in twin (exact PSD)
PASS L.cc  [countercontrol] countercontrol: at the same sample the (I, reflY) link table is not in Q3 (it is in twin only)

== S5  four-copy interface: transports and uniform SEP
PASS F.t3  [identity] token-3 chart: fourVal X (actT r Y) E (actT r F) = fourVal X Y E F and famII e (actT r f) L (actT r L') = famII e f L L', symbolic (FCC(Q3,twin,Q3,twin) <=> FCC(Q3,Q3,Q3,Q3), with Dadj for the duals)
PASS F.t12  [identity] tokens-1,2 chart: fourVal (actT r X) (actC r Y) (actT r E) (actC r F) = fourVal X Y E F and the famII form likewise, symbolic (uniform twin <=> uniform Q3, with Dtr: actC reflY Q3 = twin)
PASS F.cc  [countercontrol] countercontrol: transporting Y but not F (token 3 read on one side only) breaks the identity
PASS F.sep  [identity] uniform SEP: fourVal (prodState x x') (prodState y y') E F = (x^ E y^)(x'^ F y'^) and the famII value on products factors the same way, symbolic (with E, F in SEP* = maxCone both factors are >= 0)

== S6  the orientation obstruction: sigma and tau, and the 16 patterns on orientation-blind cones
PASS O1  [identity] sigma: actT reflY . N(A,B,A',B') = N(A, reflY B, A', B'), symbolic locals (post-composition stays N-CLASS)
PASS O2  [identity] det(reflY B) = -det B, symbolic: sigma flips orient(A, B)
PASS O3  [identity] tau: actT reflY . N(A,B,A',B') . actT reflY = N(A, reflY B, A', B' reflY), symbolic
PASS O4  [identity] (L) and the Bell table under sigma: actC (A Rz Rx) (actT (reflY B) phiW) = actT reflY (actC (A Rz Rx) (actT B phiW)), symbolic (CONS, OQ1, SECT, PREC, hgate are sigma-invariant on actT reflY-invariant cones, with Dmax, Dsep, Dadj)
PASS O.cc  [countercontrol] countercontrol: sigma on the control side (actC reflY) changes A, not B: actC reflY . N(A,B,..) differs from N(A, reflY B, ..)
PASS O5  [enumerate] the 16 gate patterns in {g_cnot, g_D}^4 on uniform maxCone (or SEP): hcls, hadm, hcl, H and IE1 do not read the gates beyond N-CLASS, and EvenCycle holds for exactly the even patterns -- 8 even, 8 odd
PASS O6  [witness] the obstruction does not reach Q3: phiW in Q3 and actT reflY phiW = idW not in Q3 (Q3 is not actT reflY-invariant)

== S7  the matrix
model    H0  C     hgate    PREC    SECT  SECTst  SECTef     OQ1    CONS      BS      BD     PRP     TBP   SECT'
